---@class whop.events.Money
---@field amount string The amount in major units, as an exact decimal string — `"10.00"` is ten dollars. A string so no float rounds it in transit.
---@field currency string Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code, lowercase.
---@field decimals number How many decimal places the amount CARRIES — the precision the charge itself runs at.
---@field display_decimals number How many decimal places to SHOW. Usually equal to `decimals`, and deliberately not always: COP is charged in centavos but written in whole pesos, so it is `2` and `0`. Format the number in your own locale using this.

---@class whop.events.PixelValidation
---@field firing_data_ok boolean False when the event lookup failed, meaning `host_events` and `last_seen_days` are incomplete.
---@field host_events whop.events.PixelValidationHostEventsList
---@field installed boolean Whether the pixel was seen. Without a `url` this answers for the whole account: true when it has sent events recently. With a `url` it answers for THAT page only — true when the page is hosted on Whop, when the page itself has sent events recently, or when the pixel was found in its source. Events the account sent from other pages do not make a given `url` installed.
---@field last_fired_days any Event name to whole days since that event last fired, e.g. `{ "lead": 3 }`. Carries events that fired too long ago to count as installed, so you can prompt to re-check rather than report them missing.
---@field last_seen_days number|distilled.Null Days since the pixel last sent an event, within a 30-day window. `null` when it hasn't sent one in that window — which includes a pixel installed moments ago.
---@field native_tracking boolean True when `url` is hosted on Whop, so no pixel snippet is required.
---@field page_events whop.events.PixelValidationPageEventsList
---@field reachable boolean|distilled.Null Whether the page could be loaded. `null` when the request included no URL, and `true` when events settled the answer without a fetch.
---@field url string|distilled.Null The URL that was checked, after normalization. `null` when the request didn't include one.

